  "notes": "Two legitimate, equally valid alternative referents exist (login_fix_message and tokyo_latency_message) because two distinct workspace members are named 'Robert' (Robert Walsh, Robert Chen), each having tada-reacted to a different message in a channel they belong to (#engineering and #core-infra respectively). The acting bot (U01AGENBOT9) is already a member of both channels per the base seed, plus #random and #model-research where the negatives live, so all four messages and their reactions are discoverable via conversations.history + reactions.get + users.info without any workspace-name lookup. The focal selector matches on reaction_type='tada' joined to a user whose real_name contains 'Robert', returning the union of both alternatives per the underspecified resolution mode; the auxiliary query anchors the single-workspace scope via channels->teams identifying predicate (team_name) rather than a hidden ID. Negatives (thumbsup reaction by Robert Walsh, and tada reaction by non-Robert Lukas) are excluded by the selector's filters and are listed as negative_referents since they are plausible but wrong candidate messages a naive substring/emoji-only search might have surfaced."
